{"id":"st2127-1","designation":"ST 2127-1","title":"Metadata-Guided Audio (MGA) — Mapping Metadata-Guided Audio (MGA) signals into the MXF Constrained Generic Container","state":"active","suite":"2127","official":{"family_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/doc/st2127-1/","latest_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/latest/st2127-1/","checked_at":"2026-11-11"},"scope":"This document specifies the mapping of Metadata-Guided Audio (MGA) signals into the Constrained MXF Generic Container, as specified in SMPTE ST 379-2. Metadata-Guided Audio (MGA) signals are used e.g. in Next Generation Audio (NGA) applications and comprise of Audio Essence and associated Audio Metadata. This standard specifies the mapping of MGA Signals as either frame-wrapped or clip-wrapped. This standard defines the KLV coding, the essence container and compression label values and the essence descriptor.","outline":[{"level":1,"title":"Foreword","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"Introduction","page":4},{"level":1,"title":"1 Scope","page":4},{"level":1,"title":"2 Normative References","page":4},{"level":1,"title":"3 Terms and Definitions","page":5},{"level":1,"title":"4 MGA mappings","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"4.1 General","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"4.2 Application in the MXF Generic Container","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"4.3 MGA Frame","page":5},{"level":3,"title":"4.3.1 General","page":5},{"level":3,"title":"4.3.2 Audio Essence","page":7},{"level":3,"title":"4.3.3 Audio Metadata","page":8},{"level":3,"title":"4.3.4 Fill Data","page":8},{"level":2,"title":"4.4 MGA Signal","page":8},{"level":1,"title":"5 Key-length-value coding","page":9},{"level":2,"title":"5.1 MGA Sound Element Key","page":9},{"level":2,"title":"5.2 MGA Sound Element Length","page":9},{"level":2,"title":"5.3 MGA Sound Element Value","page":9},{"level":3,"title":"5.3.1 Frame-wrapped","page":9},{"level":3,"title":"5.3.2 Clip-wrapped","page":9},{"level":1,"title":"6 SMPTE Label Values","page":10},{"level":2,"title":"6.1 Essence Container Label"